      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5b8f33ea6d8cbb0cbea80416|full_name}: It wasn't ever a design decision-- we never intended for override controllers to be used in this slot. However, due to the way Unity handles scriptable objects, you can slot them in.\nIn short, never intended/considered to be possible from a design standpoint, happens to work sorta kinda not really from a technical standpoint. It would take a significant amount of additional work to make it \"properly\" work, and we'd rather focus on new features.\nI get the reason why people would want it (and it would save time for simple stuff). We'll keep that in mind for the future. No guarantees, though. We'd much rather people modify the default animation controllers provided with the SDK.\nSeems like something an editor script would make quite easy :)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
